Z||000002||Mike Murphy||11-19-2001||12:49 PM||||You can go through your local parts store and usually get best deals but they are only going to be stock units and the warranty is not as good as a long block.<P>My son just had a long block 3.1 installed in his 89 Grand Prix for $1,487 which included gasket set, water pump and oil pickup screen  plus $519 for labor.  Warranty is 3 yrs. or 100K.<P>I have a remanufatured short block with a Crane Performance Cam and Forged pistons which should give about 9.5 to 1 compression ratio.  It was going into my 87 GT but decided on a 3.1 instead.<P>Price is $975.<P>I have a local machine shop that will do a head job with a port, polish and match for around $300.<P>Mike Murphy<BR>Greencastle, Indiana||||reg||12
